uroxime axetil T"},{"label":"E","text":"Cefotetan. F"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"a0263f22b4a49e72b7e60aa981015c25733186b3"},{"id":"q-b0a7cda8c59f","stem":"The following Cephalosporins are excreted mainly through biliary tract hence no dosage adjustment is required in renal impairment","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Antimicrobials","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cefoperazone. T"},{"label":"B","text":"Cefoxin. F"},{"label":"C","text":"Cefixime. F"},{"label":"D","text":"Ceftriaxone. T"},{"label":"E","text":"Cefpofoxime proxetil. F"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"a52fb66495ef736d0afcb360e43e2fc5347f078e"},{"id":"q-43a3bd82c5a4","stem":"The following statement about Penicillins are correct","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Antimicrobials","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ampicillin and Amoxycillin are destroyed by beta-lactamase. T"},{"label":"B","text":"Flucloxacillin and Clocaxillin are resistant to beta-lactamase. T"},{"label":"C","text":"Ticarcillin is particulary effective against Pseudomonas aeruginosa. F"},{"label":"D","text":"Penicillinase-resistant penicillins are much less active than Benzyl penicillin against bacteria species which do not produce beta lactamase. T"},{"label":"E","text":"Benzylpenicillin is very potent and is the drug of choice for Lancefield group A Streptococcal infections examples erysiplelas, scarlet fever. T"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"4b3bf20988d462eab463dd79728226a72a463173"},{"id":"q-6e6b93817c4c","stem":"The following statement about Imipenem is most accurate","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The drug has a narrow spectrum of antibacterial action. F"},{"label":"B","text":"It is used in fixed combination with sulbutamol. F"},{"label":"C","text":"Imipenem is highly susceptible to beta-lactamase produced by Enterobacteria species. F"},{"label":"D","text":"In renal dysfunction, dasage reductions are necessary to avoid seizures. T"},{"label":"E","text":"Imipenem is active against methicilin-resistant Staphyococci. F"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"c5bc5911c5663b5f60da581b7d5429eed1860b39"},{"id":"q-5cd3a25e08fe","stem":"The clinical indications of Fluoroquinolones include the following.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Antimicrobials","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ciprofloxacin or Ofloxacin is occasionally usual for the treatment of tuberculosis and atypical mycobacteria infection. T FROM LUCAS TO LUHIGO,DOGO SOMA HAYO MASWALI YATAKUSAIDIA,ALWAYS TOGETHER BROTHER,I LOVE YOU YOUNG BROTHER 61"},{"label":"B","text":"Levofloxacin and Sparfloxacin are used in increase singly for the treatment of upper and lower respiratory tract infection. T"},{"label":"C","text":"Ciprofloxacin Ofloxacin and Norfloxacin are effective for bacterial diarrhea caused by Shigella, toxigenic E.coli, or Camphylobacter. T"},{"label":"D","text":"Ofloxacin is effective for Chlamydial urethritis or cevitis. T"},{"label":"E","text":"Ciprofloxacin and Ofloxacin are effective for gonococcal infection including disseminated disease. T"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"2994f55bf73da523b0deba3a5d5020ac6a124b1b"},{"id":"q-f9e7b0e45ece","stem":"The following statement about Flouroquinolones are accurate","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Trovafloxacin has been associated rarely with acute nephrotoxicity which has led to restricted indications for use of this drug. F"},{"label":"B","text":"Grepafloxacin with increased activity against gram negative organisms was withdrawn by manufactures shortly after approval because of serious bone marrow depression it caused. F"},{"label":"C","text":"Concomitant administration of Theophylline and Quinolone can lead to elevated level of Theophylline with risk of toxic effects especially seizures. T"},{"label":"D","text":"Fluoroquinolones are contraindicated in nursing mothers. T"},{"label":"E","text":"Trovafloxacin and Moxifloxacin are non renally cleared and so dose adjustment in renal failure is not necessary. T"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"3ac46983549586bc93ed94b2c445baa1797b26fb"},{"id":"q-628eed967103","stem":"Gentamicin an aminoglycoside","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Antimicrobials","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Is effective in pneumococcal pneumonia. F"},{"label":"B","text":"Is poorly absorbed from the gut. T"},{"label":"C","text":"Has a half-life of 12 hours if renal function is normal. F"},{"label":"D","text":"Penetrates poorly into CSF. T"},{"label":"E","text":"Causes irreversible eight nerve damage. T"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"ad2bbcfb8ffdc81b8555b3c530a76cb2ca89d406"},{"id":"q-fffb7488842c","stem":"Chloramphenical is u