},{"label":"B","text":"40 mins"},{"label":"C","text":"1 hour"},{"label":"D","text":"2 hours"},{"label":"E","text":"6 hours Match the body compartment with the volume, assuming a 70kg male patient:"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Embryology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-297dfb4f3272","stem":"6) If protein plasma binding is decreased, how will volume of distribution be affected?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Increased"},{"label":"B","text":"Decreased"},{"label":"C","text":"Not changed"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-14324353351c","stem":"7) 400 mg of a drug is administered to a patient and the drug is later measured in plasma to be 1 μg/ml. What is the apparent volume of distribution (Vd)?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics","options":[{"label":"A","text":"0.04 L"},{"label":"B","text":"0.4 L"},{"label":"C","text":"4 L"},{"label":"D","text":"40 L"},{"label":"E","text":"400 L"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourc