,"flags":["topic_generic","duplicate_option_text"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_text","prior_structural_review_flag","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0d7dc22c582c","stem":"3) Which of the following is most useful in determining the rate of elimination of a drug, in general?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Drug concentration in urine (renal elimination)"},{"label":"B","text":"Drug concentration in stool (bilary elimination)"},{"label":"C","text":"Drug concentration in blood"},{"label":"D","text":"Drug concentration in brain"},{"label":"E","text":"Drug oxidation rate"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"]},{"id":"q-f99037f2996d","stem":"1) For first-order drug elimination, half-life t(1/2) is ____ at two places on the curve and a constant ____ is lost per unit time.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Equal; Amount"},{"label":"B","text":"Equal; Percentage"},{"label":"C","text":"Not equal; Amount"},{"label":"D","text":"Not equal; Percentage"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-63bf7ea44a6d","stem":"2) For first-order drug elimination, given the half-life equation of t(1/2) = (0.693 * Vd) / CL, how many half-lives would be necessary to reach steady state (≈95%) without a loading dose?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 to 2"},{"label":"B","text":"2 to 3"},{"label":"C","text":"3 to 4"},{"label":"D","text":"4 to 5"},{"label":"E","text":"5 to 6"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-dcaa5094af48","stem":"3) Which of the following is NOT a drug exhibiting zero-order elimination kinetics?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Pharmacokinetics and Dynamics","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Aspirin"},{"label":"B","text":"Morphine"},{"label":"C","text":"Phenytoin"},{"label":"D","text":"ETOH"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pha