 all treatment conditions?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Single-blind study"},{"label":"B","text":"Double-blind study"},{"label":"C","text":"Placebo (negative-control)"},{"label":"D","text":"Positive-control"},{"label":"E","text":"Crossover study"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-028c0333d926","stem":"3) What type of study for an IND involves comparison with a placebo and another previously tested drug?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Single-blind study"},{"label":"B","text":"Double-blind study"},{"label":"C","text":"Placebo (negative-control)"},{"label":"D","text":"Positive-control"},{"label":"E","text":"Crossover study"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1b788525bd00","stem":"4) What clinical trial phase involves many patients and often a double-blind study with the purpose to further explore the beneficial action of the drug and toxicities?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Phase 1"},{"label":"B","text":"Phase 2"},{"label":"C","text":"Phase 3"},{"label":"D","text":"Phase 4"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-19ebe60f4091","stem":"5) What clinical trial phase involves single- or double-blind studies under very controlled conditions with the purpose to determine therapeutic effect at tolerated doses?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Phase 1"},{"label":"B","text":"Phase 2"},{"label":"C","text":"Phase 3"},{"label":"D","text":"Phase 4"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c4b6a2a8e555","stem":"6) What clinical trial phase involves submitting a New Drug Application (NDA), monitoring, and reporting by clinicians using the drug?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Phase 1"},{"label":"B","text":"Phase 2"},{"label":"C","text":"Phase 3"},{"label":"D","text":"Phase 4"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTruste