lex, whereas a1. Alpha1 agonists—Alpha1 agonists (eg, phenylephrine) con- pure β agonist (eg, isoproterenol) almost always increases the rate.tract vascular smooth muscle, especially in skin and splanchnic The diastolic blood pressure is affected mainly by peripheralblood vessels, and increase peripheral vascular resistance and vascular resistance and the heart rate. (The heart rate is importantvenous pressure. Because these drugs increase blood pressure, because the diastolic interval determines the outflow of bloodthey often evoke a compensatory reflex bradycardia. from the arterial compartment.) The adrenoceptors with the greatest effects on vascular resistance are α and β2 receptors. The2. Alpha2 agonists—Alpha2 agonists (eg, clonidine) cause pulse pressure (the systolic minus the diastolic pressure) is deter- vasoconstriction when administered intravenously or topically mined mainly by the stroke volume (a function of force of cardiac (eg, as a nasal spray), but when given orally they accumulate in contraction), which is influenced by β1 receptors. The systolicthe CNS and reduce sympathetic outflow and blood pressure as pressure is the sum of the diastolic and the pulse pressures and is described in Chapter 11. therefore a function of both α and β effects."}],"priority":2,"status":"quarantine","flags":["probable_document_or_multiple_questions","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"General Pharmacology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"quarantine","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","long_option_manual_review","long_stem_manual_review","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","probable_document_or_multiple_questions","too_many_options"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-8a9a7c3e572d","stem":"Dopamine—Dopamine causes vas