xt). The reduction in heart rate caused by norepinephrine is the result of baroreceptor reflex activation of vagal outflow to the heart. CLINICAL USES are in current use for glaucoma and include apraclonidine and brimonidine. As noted, the α2-selective agonists appear to reduce Pharmacokinetic characteristics and clinical applications of selected aqueous synthesis. See Table 10–3 for a summary of drugs used sympathomimetics are shown in the Drug Summary Table. in glaucoma."},{"label":"A","text":"Anaphylaxis D. Bronchi Epinephrine is the drug of choice for the immediate treatment The β agonists, especially the β2-selective agonists, are drugs of of anaphylactic shock because it is an effective physiologic antago- choice in the treatment of acute asthmatic bronchoconstriction. nist of many of the mediators of anaphylaxis. Antihistamines and The short-acting β2-selective agonists (eg, albuterol, metapro- corticosteroids may also be used, but these agents are neither as terenol, terbutaline) are not recommended for prophylaxis, but efficacious as epinephrine nor as rapid acting. they are safe and effective and may be lifesaving in the treatment of bronchospasm. Much longer-acting β2-selective agonists, sal- meterol, formoterol, and indacaterol are used in combination"},{"label":"B","text":"Central Nervous System with corticosteroids for prophylaxis; they are not indicated for the The phenylisopropylamines such as amphetamine are widely treatment of acute symptoms, see Chapter 20. used and abused for their CNS effects. Legitimate indications include narcolepsy and, with appropriate adjuncts, weight reduc- E. Cardiovascular Applications tion. The anorexiant effect may be helpful in initiating weight loss"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"General Pharmacology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus"