on in this hyperpolarization- 5. A new 60-year-old patient presents to the medical clinic with induced inward pacemaker current results in decreased heart rate hypertension and angina. In considering adverse effects of possible drugs for these conditions, you note that an adverseand consequently decreased cardiac work. effect that nitroglycerin and prazosin have in common is (A) Bradycardia NONPHARMACOLOGIC THERAPY (B) Impaired sexual function (C) Lupus erythematosus syndrome (D) Orthostatic hypotension Myocardial revascularization by coronary artery bypass grafting (E) Throbbing headache (CABG) and percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) are extremely important in the treatment of severe 6. A man is admitted to the emergency department with a brownish cyanotic appearance, marked shortness of breath,angina. These are the only methods capable of consistently and hypotension. Which of the following is most likely to increasing coronary flow in atherosclerotic angina and increasing the double product. (A) Amyl nitrite (B) Isosorbide dinitrate (C) Isosorbide mononitrate QUESTIONS (D) Nitroglycerin (E) Sodium cyanide Questions 1–4. A 60-year-old man presents to his primary care physician with a complaint of severe chest pain when he walks 7. Another patient is admitted to the emergency department uphill to his home in cold weather. The pain disappears when he after a drug overdose. He is noted to have hypotension and rests. After evaluation and discussion of treatment options, a deci- severe tachycardia. He has been receiving therapy for hyper- sion is made to treat him with nitroglycerin. tension and angina. Which of the following drugs often"}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicat