nduce or inhibit drug-metabolizing enzymes to a very significant extent. Smoking is a common cause of enzyme induction 2. Enzyme inhibition—A few common inhibitors and the in the liver and lung and may increase the metabolism of some drugs. drugs whose metabolism is diminished are listed in Table 4–4. Because the rate of biotransformation is often the primary determi­ The inhibitors of drug metabolism most likely to be involved nant of clearance, variations in drug metabolism must be considered in serious drug interactions are amiodarone, cimetidine, carefully when designing or modifying a dosage regimen. furanocoumarins present in grapefruit juice, azole antifungals, and the HIV protease inhibitor ritonavir. Suicide inhibitors"},{"label":"A","text":"Genetic Factors are drugs that are metabolized to products that irreversibly Several drug-metabolizing systems have long been known to inhibit the metabolizing enzyme. Such agents include ethinyl differ among families or populations in genetically determined estradiol, norethindrone, spironolactone, secobarbital, allopu­ ways. Because recent advances in genomic techniques are making rinol, fluroxene, and propylthiouracil. Metabolism may also be it possible to screen for a huge variety of polymorphisms, it is decreased by pharmacodynamic factors such as a reduction in expected that pharmacogenomics will become an important part blood flow to the metabolizing organ (eg, propranolol reduces of patient evaluation in the near future, influencing both drug hepatic blood flow). choice and drug dosing (see Chapter 5)."}],"priority":2,"status":"quarantine","flags":["probable_document_or_multiple_questions","topic_generic","duplicate_option_labels","requires_visual_review"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":true,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Cardiovascular Drugs · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"quarantine","auditFlags":["du